// Mutates self and returns self by reference -- see
// tests/06_structs/23_self_pointer_chaining.tr for why this (rather than a
// by-value `Builder` return) is the idiomatic way to support chaining, and
// for why the return type is `&Builder` (issue #238: a plain function may
// never return a raw ptr/T* type, even inside `unsafe { }` -- it used to
// buffer to split a long line. At the end of input it returns what it has,
// which is "" when nothing is left: an empty line and the end of input read
// the same.
